{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.CrossProduct","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Sqrt"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.depletionKernel_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.depletionKernel_witness","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/GeometricDepletion.lean#L204-L210","doc":"Non-vacuity witness: `D` is not identically zero on unit vectors.\nWith `e₁ = (1,1,1)/√3`, `e₂ = (1,0,0)`, `e₃ = (0,1,0)` the value is `1/3`.\n`D` is homogeneous of degree 2 in `e₁`, so the unnormalised `e₁ = (1,1,1)` gives `D = 1`,\nwhich stays rational. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.abs_depletionKernel_le_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.abs_depletionKernel_le_unit","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/GeometricDepletion.lean#L194-L202","doc":"**Pointwise geometric depletion.** For unit vectors,\n`|D(e₁, e₂, e₃)| ≤ min(‖e₃ - e₂‖, ‖e₃ + e₂‖)` in the Euclidean norm. This is\nthe kernel-level reason a direction field that is Lipschitz *as a line field*\ndepletes vortex stretching. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.euclidNorm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.euclidNorm","kind":"def","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/GeometricDepletion.lean#L190-L192","doc":"Euclidean norm on `Fin 3 → ℝ` (the ambient `‖·‖` on this type is the sup\nnorm, so the Euclidean one is written out). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.depletionKernel_sq_le_unit_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.depletionKernel_sq_le_unit_add","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/GeometricDepletion.lean#L180-L184","doc":"Unit-vector depletion, anti-aligned side: `D(e₁, e₂, e₃)² ≤ |e₃ + e₂|²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.depletionKernel_sq_le_unit_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.depletionKernel_sq_le_unit_sub","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/GeometricDepletion.lean#L174-L178","doc":"Unit-vector depletion: `D(e₁, e₂, e₃)² ≤ |e₃ - e₂|²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.cross_sq_le_add_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.cross_sq_le_add_unit","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/GeometricDepletion.lean#L166-L172","doc":"For unit vectors, `|e₂ × e₃|² ≤ |e₃ + e₂|²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.cross_sq_le_sub_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.cross_sq_le_sub_unit","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/GeometricDepletion.lean#L158-L164","doc":"For unit vectors, `|e₂ × e₃|² ≤ |e₃ - e₂|²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.depletionKernel_sq_le_cross_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.depletionKernel_sq_le_cross_unit","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/GeometricDepletion.lean#L144-L156","doc":"Sharp unit form: for unit `e₁, e₃`, `D² ≤ |e₂ × e₃|²`, which for unit `e₂`\nis `sin² ∠(e₂, e₃)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.depletionKernel_sq_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.depletionKernel_sq_le","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/GeometricDepletion.lean#L134-L142","doc":"Homogeneous Lipschitz-type bound on the depletion kernel:\n`D(e₁, e₂, e₃)² ≤ |e₁|⁴ |e₂|² |e₃|² |e₃ - e₂|²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.triple_sq_le_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.triple_sq_le_sub","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/GeometricDepletion.lean#L124-L132","doc":"Hadamard in dimension 3, with the depletion shift:\n`det(e₁, e₂, e₃)² ≤ |e₁|² |e₂|² |e₃ - e₂|²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.triple_sq_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.triple_sq_le","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/GeometricDepletion.lean#L119-L122","doc":"`det(e₁, e₂, e₃)² ≤ |e₁|² |e₂ × e₃|²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.dot_sq_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.dot_sq_le","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/GeometricDepletion.lean#L113-L117","doc":"Cauchy–Schwarz for the dot product on `Fin 3 → R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.dot_self_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.dot_self_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/GeometricDepletion.lean#L109-L111","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.cross_dot_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.cross_dot_self","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/GeometricDepletion.lean#L98-L101","doc":"Lagrange's identity: `|b × c|² = |b|²|c|² - (b·c)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.triple_sub_second","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.triple_sub_second","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/GeometricDepletion.lean#L93-L96","doc":"`det(e₁, e₂, e₃) = det(e₁, e₂, e₃ - e₂)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.depletionKernel_neg_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.depletionKernel_neg_neg","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/GeometricDepletion.lean#L85-L91","doc":"A global sign flip of the direction field **reverses** `D`. This matches the\nPDE: `ω ↦ -ω` is `u ↦ -u`, which reverses the strain `S` and with it the\nstretching rate `α = ξ·Sξ`. The sign belongs to the flow, not to the line field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.depletionKernel_neg_third","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.depletionKernel_neg_third","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/GeometricDepletion.lean#L80-L83","doc":"`D` is even in its third slot. The kernel sees only the line `[ξ(x+y)]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.depletionKernel_neg_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.depletionKernel_neg_self","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/GeometricDepletion.lean#L75-L78","doc":"Anti-aligned directions: `D(e₁, e₂, -e₂) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.depletionKernel_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.depletionKernel_self","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/GeometricDepletion.lean#L71-L73","doc":"Aligned directions: `D(e₁, e₂, e₂) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.triple_eq_det","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.triple_eq_det","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/GeometricDepletion.lean#L67-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.depletionKernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.depletionKernel","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/GeometricDepletion.lean#L64-L65","doc":"Constantin's geometric kernel `D(e₁, e₂, e₃) = (e₁·e₃) · det(e₁, e₂, e₃)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.triple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.GeometricDepletion.triple","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/GeometricDepletion.lean#L61-L62","doc":"The scalar triple product `det(e₁, e₂, e₃) = e₁ · (e₂ × e₃)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}